# Across and past in Russian: перейти через, пройти мимо
subtitle: "Tom's way to work in Petersburg: one metro stop, across the street, past the café and in. Each Russian verb front comes with its own little word."
tags: ["russian","verbs of motion","russian prefixes","перейти","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/motion-prefixes","grammar/prepositions","vocabulary/the-city"]
thumb: "band \"Across and past in Russian\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Two new chairs in Russian: два новых стула","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/108-russian-two-chairs.cast"}

## Across and past in Russian: перейти через, пройти мимо
stress: all
level: basic
